---
alwaysApply: false
---

global_requirements:
  - Cursor must ALWAYS ask necessary clarifying questions
    before generating code (unless developer says "no questions").
  - Output must ALWAYS match the installed Angular version,
    TypeScript version, Ant Design version, and any UI framework
    found in:
        • package.json
        • package-lock.json
        • angular.json
  - NEVER hallucinate missing imports, methods, modules, or APIs.
  - ALWAYS use existing project structure, naming patterns, and
    coding standards automatically.
  - ALWAYS generate fully working, production-ready, minimal and
    clean Angular code.
  - ALWAYS follow Angular best practices:
        • Standalone components only if project uses them
        • Modules only if project uses modules
        • Strong typing everywhere
        • Use OnPush if the project follows it
        • Correct import paths and folder structure

framework_detection:
  angular:
    enable: true
  ant_design:
    detect_from_installed_packages: true
    required_packages:
      - ng-zorro-antd
  tailwind:
    detect_from_angular_json: true
  bootstrap:
    detect_from_styles_in_angular_json: true

ui_library_rules:
  when_ant_design_installed:
    - Prefer AntD components when generating UI
    - Use official AntD syntax, imports, modules, and services
    - Do NOT use any component not included in the installed version
  when_ant_design_not_installed:
    - NEVER generate AntD components
    - Use only Angular built-in features
    - Use developer’s chosen styling method (CSS/Tailwind/Bootstrap)

prompt_files:
  - component-generator.prompt
  - module-generator.prompt
  - route-generator.prompt
  - list-table.prompt
  - drawer.prompt
  - modal.prompt
  - ant-ui.prompt

default_behavior:
  - When ANY prompt file is used, Cursor must:
        1. Detect Angular version
        2. Detect UI library (AntD/Tailwind/Bootstrap/None)
        3. Ask developer required questions
        4. Generate correct, clean code
        5. Provide all needed imports & scaffolding
        6. Prevent unused code or missing modules
  - For table/list/drawer/modal:
        • Ask pagination type, filtering, sorting, drawer/modal mode
  - For routing:
        • Ask path, lazy loading, guards, redirects
  - For components:
        • Ask type (basic/table/form/drawer/modal)
        • Ask UI library choice
  - For UI components:
        • Ask component type + required props + design

strict_rules:
  - Do NOT create unnecessary files.
  - Do NOT produce code that fails compilation.
  - Do NOT guess module names or import paths.
  - Do NOT generate UI unless requested.
  - Do NOT output AntD code if AntD is not installed.
  - Do NOT skip Router/Forms/HttpClient imports when required.
  - Do NOT change stylesheet type (css ↔ scss).
  - Do NOT delete existing .css or .scss files.
  - When updating styles: MERGE, never overwrite.

ask_these_questions_every_time:
  - “Which Angular component/module should this integrate with?”
  - “Ant Design UI or plain Angular UI?”
  - “Standalone or NgModule-based?”
  - “Tailwind/Bootstrap or plain CSS?”
  - “Specific layout, behavior, or interactions?”
  - “Generate service/model/route if missing?”

output_quality_rules:
  - Code must be:
      • Clean, readable
      • Best-practice aligned
      • Fully typed
      • Zero warnings
      • Zero errors
  - Include interfaces for inputs/outputs
  - Provide minimal CSS for layout
  - Follow Angular official naming conventions

# =========================================================
# UPDATED SECTION — FIXED CSS/SCSS PROBLEM
# =========================================================

project_state_detection:
  detect_existing_files: true

  rules:
    - Inspect and analyze existing component files:
        • *.component.ts
        • *.component.html
        • *.component.css
        • *.component.scss
    - Detect EXACT stylesheet used by component:
        • If file ends with `.component.css`, ALWAYS generate CSS only.
        • If file ends with `.component.scss`, ALWAYS generate SCSS only.
    - When updating:
        • NEVER overwrite existing style files
        • NEVER convert CSS to SCSS or SCSS to CSS
        • NEVER delete CSS/SCSS files
        • Merge new styles into existing stylesheet safely
        • Maintain original formatting and indentation
    - Preserve:
        • Services
        • Inputs/Outputs
        • Selectors
        • ChangeDetectionStrategy
        • Existing logic
        • Existing styling frameworks (CSS/Tailwind/Bootstrap)

  detect_ui_libraries:
    - Detect installed libraries from:
        • package.json
        • angular.json (styles/scripts)
        • node_modules
    - Supported detection:
        • Ant Design (ng-zorro-antd)
        • Tailwind CSS
        • Bootstrap
    - When NONE detected:
        • Ask: “No UI library found. Install Ant Design, Tailwind,
          Bootstrap, or continue with plain Angular?”

  detect_css_frameworks:
    - Check angular.json for Tailwind/Bootstrap config
    - Check component CSS/SCSS for utility classes
    - Maintain styling consistency across generated code

  version_validation:
    - Validate Angular, TypeScript, AntD, Tailwind, Bootstrap versions
    - Ensure output matches EXACT installed versions
    - Warn when:
        • UI library version is incompatible
        • Angular major version mismatch
        • Deprecated APIs found in existing files

# =========================================================

ui_ux_design_rules:
  global_design:
    - Follow modern UX principles: clarity, spacing, contrast, hierarchy.
    - Clean structure with consistent alignment and padding.
    - Avoid clutter; prefer simplicity.
    - Ensure accessibility: ARIA roles, keyboard nav, focus states.
    - Responsive by default for all breakpoints.
    - UI must look premium, modern, consistent.

  spacing_and_layout:
    - Use spacing scale: 24px (sections), 16px (content), 8px (micro).
    - Group related fields visually using cards/dividers.
    - Use grid/flex for balanced alignment.

  component_design:
    - Follow AntD patterns when AntD exists.
    - Button hierarchy: primary > default > link.
    - Inline validation for forms.
    - Tables must include sorting, filtering, empty state, pagination.
    - Modals/Drawers must be clean with proper sizing and clear CTAs.

  styling_principles:
    - Subtle shadow, soft borders, modern rounded corners.
    - Use palette of the installed UI library.
    - Consistent typography.

  responsiveness:
    - Components must scale well on mobile/tablet/desktop.
    - Use column or stacked layouts based on viewport width.

  interaction_patterns:
    - Disable submit buttons until form is valid.
    - Provide loading, error, and success states.
    - Never hide errors; show them clearly.

